        "Introduced U maps to urine creatinine, P to blood/serum creatinine, V to total urine volume and t to collection time. Both concentrations must be of creatinine on the same mass basis. Source mg/dL concentrations are normalized to kg/m^3, volume to m^3 and duration to seconds; no conversion literal is inlined. "
        "Mass units cancel even in the runtime's non-SI mass base: (M L^-3)*L^3 / ((M L^-3)*T)=L^3 T^-1. Source's reported 168.3 mL/min is retained as the oracle after conversion; no BSA indexing is in this equation. "
        "The no-excretion U=0 limit is admitted algebraically for a positive collected sample; zero collected volume is excluded because an assayed urine specimen is required.",
        [v("U", "Introduced U maps to Creatinine, Urine", "input", "urine_creatinine_mass_concentration", "Creatinine mass per urine volume in a representative mixed aliquot of the complete timed specimen.", "kg/m^3", "M L^-3", ctx, "Finite nonnegative; assay validity and detection limits are external. Zero denotes an ideal no-excretion limit, not proof of an assay result."),
         v("V", "Introduced V maps to Total Volume 24 Hour Urine", "input", "collected_urine_volume", "Entire urine volume from the same complete collection, not the small aliquot submitted for assay.", "m^3", "L^3", ctx, "Finite strictly positive collection volume sufficient for a valid assay specimen."),
         v("P", "Introduced P maps to Creatinine, Blood (serum)", "input", "serum_creatinine_mass_concentration", "Representative serum creatinine mass concentration matched to the collection interval.", "kg/m^3", "M L^-3", ctx, "Finite strictly positive. Same analyte/mass and compatible assay basis as U."),
         v("t", "Introduced t maps to Collection Time, Minutes", "input", "duration", "Actual continuous elapsed collection duration in seconds; source application is a complete nominal 24-hour collection with actual times recorded.", "s", "T", ctx, "Finite strictly positive; caller verifies the intended 24-hour collection profile and completeness."),
         v("C", "Introduced C maps to CRCLR", "output", "creatinine_clearance", "Measurement-derived effective serum volume cleared of creatinine per time over the collection interval; not BSA-adjusted.", "m^3/s", "L^3 T^-1", ctx, "Finite nonnegative; interpretation depends on valid sampling and representative serum concentration.")],
        ["U >= 0", "V > 0", "P > 0", "t > 0"],
        ["Source requirements: the laboratory calculation uses total timed urine volume, urine creatinine and blood creatinine; paired specimens and recorded collection interval are required.",
         "Application profile: serum P is representative over the interval, and urine U is homogeneous in the mixed complete collection; this makes U*V the total excreted creatinine mass.",
         "Population scope: this is specimen arithmetic, not a fitted age/sex model. No pediatric, pregnancy or disease-specific reference-range validity is claimed; qualified interpretation remains external."],
